  "_about": "a wandering albatross ashore: the largest seabird -- a heavy white body on short legs and big pink webbed feet, the thick neck and big head; the massive pink bill built of horny plates, the tube nostrils along its sides and the hooked yellowish tip; the immensely long, narrow wings (some 3 m across) folded into a long blackish blade, flecked white on the coverts, reaching far past the short white tail. Coats: wandering, black-browed (smaller, the dark mantle and brow, the orange-yellow bill), Laysan (dark-backed, the grey smudge round the eye). (rework/bigbirds/bigbirds.py)",
